# Python quality

- Keep the package installable via the project manifest (`pyproject.toml` / equivalent). Declare dependencies there; do not assume undeclared packages.
- Prefer `src/` layout imports when the repo uses them (e.g. `from package import ...`).
- Type public functions and dataclasses when the surrounding code already uses typing.
- Fail loudly on missing required configuration (e.g. API keys). Do not silently continue with empty credentials.
- Put tests under `tests/` with pytest. Keep unit tests offline by default (no live network); mark integration tests explicitly if they need it.
- Prefer focused tests for new behavior over broad unrelated suite churn.
- Do not log or serialize secrets.